From 82b73e10fcff2e4510203211354859efd5a72bbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:47:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] fix(cli): fail loud on an ACP model pin instead of
 falling back

Fork patch 0005. Under --acp, CLINE_MODEL at session/new and the model set
through session/set_config_option or session/set_model were resolved against
the bundled catalog; any other id was replaced without an error by the provider
default (minimax.minimax-m2.5 on Bedrock) or, for set_config_option, taken
unchecked.

- A pinned id in the catalog is kept.
- On Bedrock, an id outside the catalog is kept when the vendor can route it
  (inference-profile ARNs, application inference profiles, aws-mantle/<id>),
  checked with resolveBedrockMantleRoute, now exported from @cline/llms.
- Anything else fails with invalidParams naming the id, for example the empty
  Mantle id "aws-mantle/". A rejected change keeps the current model.
- The provider default applies only when nothing is pinned.
- A pinned id outside the catalog is listed in availableModels and the model
  config option, so currentValue is one of the options.
